  "result": "JPY and KRW invoices are now charged at their face value: ¥1,500 goes to the gateway as 1500, not 150000. `npm test` passes, 8 of 8.\n\n**Root cause:** `src/payments/gateway/payload.js` lower-cases the currency code (`jpy`) for the gateway, then passes that lower-case code to `toMinor`. The currency registry in `src/lib/currency/registry.js` only knows upper-case codes. `exponent('jpy')` missed and fell back to the default of 2 decimals, so yen and won were multiplied by 100. USD and EUR use 2 decimals anyway, so the fallback happened to be correct for them.\n\n**Fix:** In `src/lib/currency/registry.js`, `exponent`, `isSupported` and `symbol` now look codes up case-insensitively. This also covers any other caller that passes a lower-case code.\n\n**Regression tests** (in `test/charge.test.js`):\n- A JPY and a KRW charge payload, checking the amount is not multiplied by 100.\n- `toMinor` with lower-case `jpy` and `kwd`, so the exponent lookup itself is covered.\n\n**Side effect:** `isSupported('usd')` now returns true. I didn't search for callers that rely on it rejecting lower-case codes, so check that before merging.\n\nI didn't commit anything.",
